{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And their children who [do] not know, etc.</b> This division corresponds to the little ones (הטף) that He mentioned in the verse of <b>הַקְהֵל</b> (assemble). The commentator says: even though they have not yet reached the age to learn, nevertheless they shall hear and learn to fear HaShem — meaning, to train them in the fear of HaShem." "<b>And for this reason</b> it did not say in the manner that it said in the verse of <b>הַקְהֵל</b>: ״יִלְמְדוּ וְיָרְאוּ״ — which are two separate things — but rather ״וְלָמְדוּ לְיִרְאָה״, meaning that through this they shall learn fear of Heaven. And it said ״כָּל הַיָּמִים״, because when the little ones are trained from their very beginning in fear, the fear of HaShem becomes established in them all their days." "<b>And our Sages</b>, of blessed memory, said (חגיגה ג׳): and this is their language: ״And the little ones — why? To give reward to those who bring them.״ End quote. And perhaps they give a reason even for the smallest of the small who do not understand anything, for they too are included in the general category of הטף that the verse stated; and what the verse gave as a reason — ״יִשְׁמְעוּ וְלָמְדוּ״ — refers to their children who are beginning to understand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:53.262404479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}